---
description: Kotlin coding style
globs:
- "**/*.kt"
alwaysApply: true
---

Write Kotlin code in an imperative style.

Requirements:

- Use explicit if/else blocks.
- Declare variables before assigning.
- Do not use expression-bodied if/when unless requested.
- Avoid nested scope functions (let, apply, run, with, also).
- Avoid smart one-line Kotlin syntax.
- Prefer multiple simple statements over one complex expression.
- Use meaningful variable names.
- Comment each logical step.
- Optimize for readability, not brevity.
- Do not hashcode the string.